Page Object Model (POM)
1. Simple Definition (Interview Answer)

“Page Object Model is a design pattern in Selenium where each web page of an application is represented as a separate Java class. All web elements and actions on that page are stored in that class.”

2. Why POM is Used?

Without POM ❌

Locators are written in test cases
Code duplication
Hard to maintain

With POM ✅

Clean separation of test and page logic
Easy maintenance
Reusable methods
Better readability
3. Real-Time Idea

Think like this:

Login Page → LoginPage.java
Home Page  → HomePage.java
Cart Page  → CartPage.java

Each page = one class.

